        "problem": "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(7xy),$ then $\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}=$",
        "worked_solution": "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(7xy),$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(7x(y+h)).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(7x(y+h))-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(7xy)}{h}).\n$$",
